{title: I Lay It Down}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 136}

Verse 1
[B]In [Em]the Garden of [D]Gethsemane I [Em]ponder,
[B]With [B7]a [Em]sorrow unto death, to [D]You I [G]cry.
[B7]Though my [Am]calling leads me [G]onward
To the [D]suff'ring of the [D#m]cross,
[Em]I pray this [Em]cup [B]would pass me [E]by.

Verse 2
[B]I'm alone [Em]for all my friends have grown too [E]weary.
[B7]In the darkness [Em]of the hour, I [D]am undone.
[B]Yet [Bm7]again, [Am]I plead and pray,
[G]Dear Father, take this [D]cup away,
[Em7]And [Em]spare the suff'ring [B]of Your [F#]Son.

Chorus 1
[E]Must I [Gmaj7]lay [G]down my life in agony,
[D]Must I [Am]bear [Am7]all the [C]sin and shame?
[B]Must You [G]soon turn Your face away from [D]me,
As the [Am7]people [C]mock my Name?
[B]There is [Em]nothing that You cannot [A]do,
So [Am]once [C]again, I cry:
My [B7]Father, [B7]let [Em]this [Bm7]cup [D]now pass me by.
[Em]My [B]Father, [D#m]let [Em]this cup now pass me by!

Bridge
[E]Abba, Father! [Em]I [B]cry,
Must [E]I [E]be crucified?
[G]Must I [D]shed my blood [Em]upon [Em]the [B]ground?
[B7]Must [G]I be [D]led to wear [E]a thorny [B]crown?
[G]Must I face [D]the [E]coldness of [E]the tomb?
[B]Please, [Cmaj7]Father [B]must I [E]die?
[B7](Short pause)

Verse 3
[B]I [E]awaken those [E]who close [D]their eyes [Bm7]in [Em]slumber.
[B]Now the [E]hour has [Em]come; [Em7]betrayal [D]drawing [G]near.
[B7]Soon the soldiers [Am]will [Am7]descend,
[G]And all the suff'ring [D]will [D7]begin,
[Em]And my disciples [E]flee [B7]in [E]fear.

Verse 4
[B]For this [Em]moment I [E]was [D]born; I cannot [Em]falter.
[B]As the [Em]Lamb I come to [D]give my life for [G]all.
Since [Am]before the world [Am7]began,
[G]My death was in [D]our master plan,
[Em]And I must [B]answer to [D#m]the [Em]call:

Chorus 2
[E]If the [G]shadow of death must pass [D]this way,
As the [Am7]wages [C]of sin are [B]borne,
Though the [G]wrath and judgement I [D]must bear
Leave me [C]battered, bruised, and [B]torn,
If the [Em]bearing [Em7]of the cross [A]must come
Before [C]I wear the [B]crown,
I yield my life to You; I lay it down.
I yield my [Em]life to You; [D]I lay it [Em]down!
